{
    "background_story": "Joaquin was a struggling artist in 19th century Spain, known for his bold and expressive sketches. He spent most of his days observing the world around him, capturing the beauty of everyday life on paper. Joaquin's medium of choice was blacklead, which he used to create striking portraits and landscapes. His artwork often featured the working class, highlighting their struggles and triumphs. As his skills improved, Joaquin's art gained recognition, and he became a prominent figure in the local art scene. He was particularly drawn to the dramatic effects that blacklead could produce, using it to create deep shadows and rich textures. Joaquin's passion for art and his mastery of blacklead earned him a reputation as one of the most talented artists of his time.",
